  "_comment": "UnoOne offline model manifest — per-language voice models. English: sherpa-asr-en (streaming zipformer transducer int8) + sherpa-tts-en (Coqui VITS + espeak-ng-data bundled as an app asset). Indian languages (Hindi/Bengali/Tamil/Telugu/Kannada/Malayalam): sherpa-asr-whisper (a single multilingual whisper-tiny int8 tarball — the 'language' field selects the language at runtime; no Sherpa transducer exists for these) + sherpa-tts-<lang> (MMS VITS from willwade/mms-tts-multilingual-models-onnx, character frontend, no espeak). The wake-word (vad) is always English (no Indic KWS model exists). Every sha256 + sizeBytes below is stream-computed from the actual artifact bytes (no fabrication) so the installer performs strict integrity checking; gemma-local / punctuation carry URLs only (size/sha left empty — the installer still validates download completeness via the HTTP response and extraction success). The whisper tarball is a .tar.bz2 (commons-compress extracts it); its 'extractsTo' names the top directory the tar expands to (sherpa-onnx-whisper-tiny), which differs from the archive name — the strip-last-extension fallback would not work for .tar.bz2. STT and the wake-word (vad) share the same public streaming-zipformer-int8 English transducer (encoder/decoder/joiner/tokens).",
